1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,264
Meet SnapFloat.

2
00:00:01,314 --> 00:00:06,094
The Mac screenshot thumbnail, for Linux
and Windows, and then some.

3
00:00:06,733 --> 00:00:09,897
Press Print Screen, and select what you
want to share.

4
00:00:10,533 --> 00:00:12,586
Your screenshot floats in the corner.

5
00:00:12,636 --> 00:00:15,387
Nothing piles up in your Screenshots
folder.

6
00:00:16,033 --> 00:00:18,786
Drag it straight into any app, like a
chat.

7
00:00:18,836 --> 00:00:19,738
That's it.

8
00:00:20,367 --> 00:00:22,567
Click the thumbnail to mark it up.

9
00:00:22,617 --> 00:00:26,706
One click hides phone numbers, emails, and
one-time codes.

10
00:00:27,333 --> 00:00:30,027
Add arrows, numbered steps, and text.

11
00:00:30,077 --> 00:00:31,514
Then press Done.

12
00:00:32,133 --> 00:00:34,295
Need the words, not the picture?

13
00:00:34,345 --> 00:00:37,637
Drag over any part, and copy just that
text.

14
00:00:38,267 --> 00:00:41,547
Beautify gives it a clean background,
ready to post.

15
00:00:42,267 --> 00:00:42,945
Took a few?

16
00:00:42,995 --> 00:00:47,817
Combine them into one image, or hold Shift
and drag them all at once.

17
00:00:48,467 --> 00:00:49,704
Closed one too early?

18
00:00:49,754 --> 00:00:53,007
It's still there, under Recent, in the
tray menu.

19
00:00:53,633 --> 00:00:56,542
To catch a menu, use a delayed capture.

20
00:00:58,433 --> 00:00:59,423
Done with it?

21
00:00:59,473 --> 00:01:01,244
Just flick it away.

22
00:01:01,867 --> 00:01:05,600
Pick the corner, the timing, the size, and
your shortcuts.

23
00:01:06,233 --> 00:01:08,912
SnapFloat is free and open source.

24
00:01:08,962 --> 00:01:10,576
Get it on GitHub.

